{
 "schema": 1,
 "contract": {
  "doc": "Shared update-marker identity corpus (ROUND5 A7 rule 7). Every marker reader runs the 'judge' cases and every releaser the 'release' cases.",
  "format": [
   "line 1: owner pid, ASCII digits, fits u32 (else MALFORMED)",
   "line 2: started_at unix seconds, ASCII digits (else MALFORMED)",
   "line 3: ct:<digits[.digits]> owner creation time; anything else makes the marker v1",
   "lines 4+: tagged; 'delegate:<pid> ct:<ct>' (exactly one space; first well-formed one wins) and 'run:<[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,128}>' (first wins); unknown/malformed tagged lines are ignored. Writers put the delegate on line 4.",
   "per line: drop one leading BOM (line 1), one trailing CR, surrounding spaces/tabs"
  ],
  "liveness": [
   "an identity is (pid, ct); dead if the pid is not a live process (pid 0 never is)",
   "our own pid: ours only if |ct - our_ct| <= own_ct_epsilon; a no-ct claim naming our pid is a previous incarnation (dead)",
   "any other pid: live if |ct - actual| <= ct_tolerance; no recorded ct (v1) or unreadable actual ct: live only while now - started_at <= v1_max_age",
   "verdict: malformed | dead | ours (a live identity is our incarnation) | live; owner = the owner identity if live, else the delegate if live, else null"
  ],
  "release": [
   "releaser owns line 1-3 identity (exact incarnation): delete, unless a delegate that is live and not the releaser exists -> rewrite with that delegate as owner (started_at and run lines kept)",
   "releaser is the delegate: owner live -> rewrite without the delegate line; owner dead -> delete",
   "anything else: keep. Every release runs under the <marker>.lock kernel lock (A7 rule 1)"
  ],
  "live_table": "pid -> creation time of a live process; null = alive but creation time unreadable; absent = no such process. The case's own process (our_pid/our_ct, else the top-level defaults; releaser_pid/releaser_ct in release cases) is always alive with that ct.",
  "rewrite_text": "rewritten markers are canonical: '<pid>\\n<started_at>\\nct:<ct as written>\\n' then the kept run lines, each '\\n'-terminated"
 },
